sections.full_text:
(1) There is established for the Commission, a Governing Board (in this Act referred to as "the Board").
(2) The Board shall consist of —
(a) a Chairman;
(b) one person each from the Member States of the Commission, that is —
(i) Benue,
(ii) Kogi,
(iii) Kwara,
(iv) Nasarawa,
(v) Niger,
(vi) Plateau, and
(vii) Federal Territory (FCT), Abuja;
(c) three persons to represent security agencies;
(d) one representative of solid minerals and mining producing companies;
(e) one person each to represent the Federal Ministries of Finance, Environment, and Housing;
(f) the Managing Director and Executive Directors of the Commission.
(3) The Chairman and members of the Board shall be appointed by the President, subject to confirmation by the Senate.

(1) The Commission shall —
(a) formulate policies and guidelines for the development of the North Central states;
(b) conceive, plan and implement projects and programmes for sustainable development in transportation, health, education, agriculture, industrialisation, housing, water supply, electricity, and telecommunications;
(c) tackle ecological and environmental problems arising from solid mineral extraction and mining;
(d) manage and monitor funds allocated to the Commission for the reconstruction and rehabilitation of the zone.

